  "final_text": "**Not really.** The drop from 3.21 to 2.51 NCRs per 1,000 units comes almost entirely from one week that probably shouldn't count as September. If you compare like for like, CRAFT's quality was flat, and by some measures it got worse.\n\n**How the 2.51 is built**\n\nThe report's numbers match the data: August was 24 NCRs on 7,488 units (3.21 per 1,000) and September was 23 NCRs on 9,162 units (2.51). But September's figure covers five weekly buckets, and the fifth one starts 2023-09-30. That week is labelled **FY24-Q3-W01**, so it's a Q3 week and runs mostly into October.\n\n| CRAFT week | Units | NCRs | NCRs per 1,000 units |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Aug (4 weeks) | 7,488 | 24 | 3.21 |\n| Sep 02 | 1,874 | 5 | 2.67 |\n| Sep 09 | 1,624 | 4 | 2.46 |\n| Sep 16 | 1,877 | 5 | 2.66 |\n| **Sep 23** | 1,752 | **8** | **4.57**, the worst week in either month |\n| **Sep 30 (Q3-W01)** | **2,035** | **1** | **0.49** |\n\nThat last week adds 22% more units but only one NCR, which is what pulls the rate down. The NCR file ends on 2023-09-30, so NCRs raised later that week may not have been logged yet. I can't prove the week is incomplete (AURA logged 7 NCRs in it), but CRAFT never had fewer than 4 NCRs in any other week, so 1 looks like an outlier.\n\n**Comparing the same four weeks in each month**\n\n| CRAFT | August | Sep (4 weeks, without Q3-W01) |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| NCRs per 1,000 units | 3.21 | **3.09** (−4%, within normal week-to-week noise) |\n| Units affected per 1,000 units | 310 | **387** (+25%, worse) |\n\nSo CRAFT logged about the same number of NCRs per unit, but those NCRs affected more units, and the month ended on its worst week.\n\n**Other points for the decision**\n\n- **\"No other line improved\"** is technically true: AURA went 0.33 → 0.43, NEST 0.89 → 1.13 and PULSE stayed flat at 0.71. But CRAFT's \"improvement\" is the week-mix effect above, so this argument doesn't really favour CRAFT.\n- **CRAFT is still the worst line by far.** At about 3.1 NCRs per 1,000 units, it's roughly 3× NEST and 7–9× AURA, and it had the most NCRs in both months.\n- **The report already warns about the five-week September in §6.** It applied that warning to revenue but not to the quality rate the VP of Sales is quoting.\n\nIf the decision depends on \"quality is already turning,\" the data doesn't support it yet. It's worth re-running the NCR pull once the Sep 30 week is fully logged before giving CRAFT more marketing budget.",
